Dear Chris,



I take this opportunity to wish you a happy new year 2012.



As we need this converter in order to display some digital image into a PAL=
 input of a digital monitor for a demonstration purpose, we've run some tes=
t in order to test the quality of the conversion. Throughout these tests, w=
e've found some strange points about the converter :



1)  The standard HD720p (1280x720x60 Hz) is not supported at all. In this c=
ase, the OSD just indicates "IN : not supported".


2)  At the end of the odd/even fields there is a sinusoidal signal at the c=
olor carrier frequency (4,43 MHz in PAL) just before the vertical synchroni=
zation signal. The amplitude of the signal is beyond the expected values fo=
r a chrominance signal. This signal is quite disturbing as it generates two=
 visible green lines at the bottom of the screen (both on an analog or digi=
tal screen).

[cid:image002.png@01CCCF86.4ECC4940]




3)  When PAL output is selected, some luminance signal is present beyond th=
e PAL standard 'active line' time (52 =B5s) although the total line time is=
 correct (64 =B5s). This means that some of the right part of the picture i=
s missing.

[cid:image001.png@01CCCF82.8BB42980]




Would it be possible for you to check these issues, especially the first tw=
o points ?



Thank you and Best Regards,


Patrice Bastiaens
Electronics Development Engineer
